{"name":"Aragonite Grey","hex":"#948e96","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aragonite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evaporite consisting of anhydrous calcium carbonate with the chemical formula CaCO3 and occurring in pearls, shells and nacre; it is dimorphous with calcite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aragonite"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aragonite","blocks":[{"text":"Aragonite is a carbonate mineral and one of the three most common naturally occurring crystal forms of calcium carbonate, the others being calcite and vaterite. It is formed by biological and physical processes, including precipitation from marine and freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Aragonite_crystal_-_Los_Molinillos%2C_Ceunca%2C_Spain_-_4x3.6x3.5cm_100g.jpg/330px-Aragonite_crystal_-_Los_Molinillos%2C_Ceunca%2C_Spain_-_4x3.6x3.5cm_100g.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aragonite","wikidata":"Q23775"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/AragoniteFromCrystal